        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete author Theorem2.9 route: normalized universal class uv and B_i definitions, full Lemma2.7, isotropic vanishing Proposition2.10 (both author proofs), degenerate-span reduction2.11, elementary Gram lemmas2.12–2.13 and the final integral comparison. M=M_H(v) is the smooth proper fine moduli space for a positive primitive Mukai vector, v-generic polarization and a universal sheaf, with dim(M)=v.v+2>2. The selected P is a rational polynomial in normalized B_i(x_j) and tangent Chern classes and x_j belong to the Mukai lattice; its integral depends only on P and the full Gram matrix of v,x_j. Markman operator Theorem2.4 is genuinely established prior background with the source coefficient-extension explanation preserved. Twisted-universal, Bridgeland and dimension-two extensions are not selected; no separate Hilbert-reconstruction or Segre-Verlinde consequence is counted."
